{
    "background_story": "Alden was a skilled carpenter who lived in 17th-century England. He was known for his exceptional craftsmanship, particularly in creating beautiful and functional dividers for the grand estates of the time. However, Alden's life took a dramatic turn when he was commissioned to build a divider for the local church. The project sparked a controversy, as some members of the congregation believed the divider would separate the wealthy from the poor, exacerbating social tensions. Alden found himself at the center of the debate, with some hailing him as a master craftsman and others condemning him as a contributor to social inequality. Despite the backlash, Alden remained committed to his art, using his skills to create dividers that not only reflected the beauty of the church but also symbolized the complexities of the community he served.",
